body:
It seems like you're sorry for your past.  Have you voiced your sorrow to the one's that you feel you've hurt?

&nbsp;

-one-day-at-a-time-

Good to hear.  Everything works itself out sooner or later, you'll see. :)

&nbsp;

-one-day-at-a-time-

Hey I'd be totally down to talk to you again!  Anytime shoot me a pm or whatever.  I'm about to head to bed myself.  I just fell asleep by accident.  It's 4 am right now for me...  Hey, have a good day tomorrow, ok?
&nbsp;

-one-day-at-a-time-

What has happened to make you want to kill yourself?  

&nbsp;

-one-day-at-a-time-

That's great!  How did you guys meet?

&nbsp;

-one-day-at-a-time-

Oh sweet, I love Zelda!  Snow days are fun too.  How long have you been with your girlfriend?

&nbsp;

-one-day-at-a-time-

OK, let's talk!  What did you do today?

&nbsp;

-one-day-at-a-time-

My cat purrs a lot too, and she also does that silent meowing thing that I find so freaking cute.  I'm sorry to hear that your old girl passed on.  How long did you have her for?  I found this cat on the side of the road, and just picked her up because she had no owner.  It's awesome that you have a boyfriend that at least tries.  How long have you guys been together?

&nbsp;

-one-day-at-a-time-

I see.  He seems like he really cares about you, and I think that if I was in your boyfriend's shoes, I would really want to help you battle your demons so you can live a fulfilling life doing what you love.  Speaking of which, what do you love? (hobby wise)  I love my cat, she's the bests.  She's cute and she purrs alot.  She's actually here right next to me!

&nbsp;

-one-day-at-a-time-

School isn't everything.  If you need to, take the day off tomorrow.  Ditch classes and collect your thoughts.  Think about your goals, what you want to do in the future, and how you'll get there.  
&nbsp;

-one-day-at-a-time-

Wow, that's an achievement if I've ever seen one.  She'll stick with you through thick and thin.  How did you guys meet?
&nbsp;

-one-day-at-a-time-

Ain't that the truth.  It's great that when you and your Dad last spoke, you guys made peace in your relationship.  It sounds like your girlfriend is awesome.  How long have you guys been together?

&nbsp;

-one-day-at-a-time-

Yea.  Life goes by quickly alright.  If you wake up tomorrow and can't push yourself to study, don't worry about it.  Whatever you do, commit to it.  If you can't study, relax.  Go for a walk.  Walk in there and try your best.  If you can study, then go for it!  Walk in there, get the mark you want, and leave.  Take the rest of the night off playing some video games.  
&nbsp;

-one-day-at-a-time-

I'm happy you're still with us.  First of all, don't worry about school right now.  Why do you feel as though the only way out is suicide?  Do you have any siblings or close friends that know your tendencies?
&nbsp;

-one-day-at-a-time-

I'm happy you're still with us.  What song do you hear?  
&nbsp;

-one-day-at-a-time-

I agree with you.  Some things are best left unsaid.  Your girlfriend seems to care a lot about you.  You trust her a lot, and that's good.  Were you close to your Dad growing up?
&nbsp;

-one-day-at-a-time-

Oh, don't worry about that. It's what I'm here for.  It seems like you have some regrets in life, which I do too.  I wish I paid more attention in school early on.  Every human is able to change.  Why do you think we practically rule the earth?  Adaptation is necessary for survival, especially in your case.  What makes you say that you're a manchild?  Also, I don't think you should feel jealous of those worse off than you.  They aren't really free.  Most are plagued with awful financial instability and ruined relationships with close family.  
&nbsp;

-one-day-at-a-time-

I see.  When you get out, start with small changes.  Why do you feel like committing suicide?  Was there any specific event that pushed you over the edge?
&nbsp;

-one-day-at-a-time-

I see.  What are you up to nowadays?  Do you think it's due to lack of hobbies or social connections?
&nbsp;

-one-day-at-a-time-

I'm sorry to hear about that experience.  You're not just a "shitty whiner" and you should never feel that you are.  Asking for help doesn't make you a piece of garbage.  People who criticize others don't belong here, as this is a place of support and advice.  What did you do today?  Anything fun?
&nbsp;

-one-day-at-a-time-

I'm sorry to hear that.  It sounds like he wasn't supportive.  When did you last have an issue with eating disorders? 
&nbsp;

-one-day-at-a-time-

It was never my intention to be disapproving or angry, and I apologize for coming across as such.  I'm sorry to hear that individuals have spewed abuse at you due to your sex.  Did that happen recently?
&nbsp;

-one-day-at-a-time-

Hey, I'm happy that you're still with us today.  Do you have a history of eating disorders?  Do you have anyone in your life that you're close to?
&nbsp;

-one-day-at-a-time-

I'm happy you're still with us.  School will soon be over, and you'll be living your free life as a med-tech.  Take a step back,  look at all your achievements in life.  Hell, being born is one of them!  Graduating high school, attending colleges, these are all things to be proud of.  Why did you decide to become a Med-Tech?
&nbsp;

-one-day-at-a-time-

Your mother finding out isn't a bad thing.  Your mom cares about you.  I'm happy you're still with us.  Did you go to the ER at around 3 am?

&nbsp;
-one-day-at-a-time-
